# Day 08 addition. Three kinds of export this tool produces that should not
# reach a repository, and one that should.
#
# A DR FINDINGS EXPORT is an inventory of exactly which of your recovery paths
# do not work, with resource ids attached. It is also, more specifically than
# most audit output, a schedule: it tells a reader when your last recovery
# point was taken and therefore how long they have before a restore becomes
# cheap for you.
#
# RESTORE AND BACKUP JOB LISTINGS carry the same information in rawer form.
#
# CHAOS AND WORKFLOW EXECUTION OUTPUT contains instance ids, subnet ids and
# NACL association ids — a map of what to break and how.
#
# WHAT SHOULD BE COMMITTED, and is deliberately not ignored: rto-measurements.md.
# Your measured RTO and RPO, dated. It is the single most valuable artefact
# this day produces, and an RTO without a date is an RTO from an architecture
# that no longer exists.
dr-findings.json
dr-findings-*.json
dr-audit-*.json
restore-*.json
snapshots-*.json
backup-jobs-*.json
chaos-*.json
execution-history-*.json
failover-evidence/
